      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The main understandability issues are:\n1. Many unused data provider methods (only `data_samples` is used by the actual test)\n2. Dozens of unused imports \n3. `data_samples` is formatted as one long unreadable line\n\nI'll create a cleaned-up version that keeps only what the test actually uses and reformats the data for readability.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data provider methods and imports, and reformats the `data_samples` table with one entry per line and grouped comments explaining each scenario (year 1 basics, Sol/July boundary, leap year handling, century years, etc.), making the test's intent immediately clear."
